WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.560
The first trailer for Marvel's Ant-Man and
the Wasp is here, and while it might contain

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:09.559
exactly zero hints about what's to come in
the MCU movies that precede it — namely,

00:00:09.559 --> 00:00:14.070
Black Panther and The Avengers: Infinity War
— there are plenty of clues about what lies

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:16.949
ahead for its title characters in the second
Ant-Man movie.

00:00:16.949 --> 00:00:21.430
So, pull out your magnifying glasses and search
along with us as we break down some of the

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:26.150
smallest details to be found in the first
trailer for Ant-Man and the Wasp.

00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:27.990
A new Ant-thony

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:32.250
One of the saddest moments in Ant-Man was
certainly the loss of Ant-thony, Scott Lang's

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:35.829
trusty winged ant pal who carried him through
trials large and small.

00:00:35.829 --> 00:00:39.790
The creature was well-trained, quirky, and
had a knack for arriving right in the nick

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:40.790
of time.

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:44.800
However, with Hope van Dyne's new Wasp suit
equipped with its own set of wings, Scott's

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:47.559
gonna need some aerial transportation for
the new flick himself.

00:00:47.559 --> 00:00:50.320
"So, I take it you didn't have that tech available
for me?"

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:51.320
"No, I did."

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:55.710
So, as we see in the trailer, he'll have to
let his memory of Ant-thony go and make a

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:59.320
new pal from the Formicidae family to buzz
around town with.

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:04.269
Frankly, Ant-thony 2.0 could be from the original's
own colony for how much they look alike, and

00:01:04.269 --> 00:01:09.700
what's even better is, it looks Lang's new
ride can keep pace with the Wasp, too.

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:11.240
Here's Ghost

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:15.130
We don't know for sure whether Ghost, portrayed
by Hannah John-Kamen, will be the biggest

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:16.799
bad of Ant-Man and the Wasp.

00:01:16.799 --> 00:01:20.690
But we do know that the mysterious character
will be coming along to spook our insectoid

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:21.690
heroes a bit.

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:25.700
The trailer offers not one but two glimpses
of the villainess in action.

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:30.090
In the first sighting, we see Ghost's hand,
radiating with trippy energy from that white

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.120
stealth suit.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:35.880
In the second shot of the character, we see
Ghost in a full slate gray costume, concealing

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:40.360
any trace of her humanity and leaving us instead
with the red-eyed antagonist.

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:42.369
Behold, Goliath

00:01:42.369 --> 00:01:46.960
Another first-glimpse of a new MCU character
featured in the Ant-Man and the Wasp trailer

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:52.280
is that of Bill Foster a.k.a. Goliath, a.k.a.
comics' second Giant-Man, played by Laurence

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:55.009
Fishburne, in what looks like Hank Pym's lab.

00:01:55.009 --> 00:01:59.130
It's not clear whether Foster will be in his
pre- or post-Goliath glory days by the time

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:03.700
he arrives in the Ant-Man sequel, but Fishburne
has hinted that he'll be both a "hero" and

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:05.280
scientist in the movie.

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:09.850
Whether that means he's retired his super
suit or not remains to be seen.

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:10.850
Super size me

00:02:10.850 --> 00:02:15.270
It looks like Giant-Man will be making a comeback
in Ant-Man and the Wasp as well.

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:19.300
Scott Lang usually uses his power to shrink
down to a fun-sized superhero.

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:23.590
But in Captain America: Civil War, he tried
his hand at blowing up to fight all Cap's

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:24.590
frenemies.

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:28.220
Ant-Man might've needed some fresh fruit after
it was all said and done to recover from the

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:31.460
experience, but for the most part he handled
himself just fine.

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:35.880
From the looks of this trailer, he'll be giving
Bay Area folks quite a surprise when he emerges

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:38.720
from the water in hypersize for some reason.

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:42.830
Maybe his suit's regulator gets out of whack
again, but Hank Pym should probably develop

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:47.600
a memory-erasure device next because this
is one sight San Franciscans are not likely

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:48.280
to forget.

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:49.380
"I do some dumb things."

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:51.900
Missing in action

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:56.560
Two of the most intriguing cast additions
for Ant-Man and the Wasp are Michelle Pfeiffer

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:01.920
as Janet van Dyne a.k.a. the original Wasp,
and Walton Goggins as Sonny Burch, a smarmy

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:03.340
weapons developer.

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:07.510
It's expected that, thanks to Scott Lang's
prior visit to the Quantum Realm, Hank Pym's

00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:12.590
going to order up a mission to get the original
Wasp back from said plane of micro-existence,

00:03:12.590 --> 00:03:14.140
however long that might take.

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:18.360
The trailer betrays none of that plotline,
however, and it also tells us nothing about

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:19.870
what to expect from Burch.

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:24.620
In the comics, he's a relatively small character
who gets into a tiff with Tony Stark's company.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:28.550
But since Iron Man isn't expected to have
anything to do with this movie, the running

00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:33.040
theory is that he'll be taking over for the
late Darren Cross a.k.a. Yellowjacket over

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:34.040
at Cross Technologies.

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:37.910
We'll have to wait for the film, or at least
a more revealing trailer, to find out more

00:03:37.910 --> 00:03:42.950
about either of these theory threads, but
clearly, Marvel's keeping both of these exciting

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:45.700
character debuts close to the chest for now.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:47.570
The microscopic realm

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:52.260
Our title heroes might not make way to the
Quantum Realm just yet in the film's trailer,

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:56.370
but it does look like at least someone will
be shrinking down to the microscopic plane.

00:03:56.370 --> 00:04:00.790
In one snapshot from the trailer, the team's
rocket-submarine can be seen drifting through

00:04:00.790 --> 00:04:03.090
a cloud of tardigrades, of all things.

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:07.680
Since the micro-animals are known to be water-dwelling
creatures, we can surmise that Hank &amp; Co.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:11.820
are going to be travelling somewhere wet before
getting to an even tinier realm.

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:14.690
Any excuse to show adorable water bears, right?

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:16.310
Thanks for watching!

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:19.010
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:19.010 --> 00:04:21.380
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

